So You Want To Build A Ghostwheel?  NEWS, newest first

* The whole book, draft 1 (2026-11-03)

** Seventeen spreads in two parts, with Chad's
three visits.  Part One is how we say things;
Part Two is how a ghostwheel wakes up.  Part
Two follows the run-levels, which is the plan's
lean on its fork F1, not yet Corwin's ruling.

** Facing pages, like a paper book.  The title
page has the dedication facing it; after that,
the picture page sits on the left and the
fuller page on the right.  The words on each
picture page go where they lead the eye.

** A map of the shop, inside the back cover and
under M: a floor plan, a roguelike's tiles, and
a board of cards.

** 159 witness rows behind 126 atoms.  Ten of
the atoms have rows from two hands; where those
hands differ, both rows are kept.

* The pilot (2026-11-03)

** Chad's first visit, Door and Letters, read
in two takes (the company, and the lap reader)
as a video, an mp3, captions and a slide deck.
